derivations.claim:
The invariant identity is $\pi=\pi K_0+p
u$. Iteration gives $\pi=p\sum_{j=0}^{n-1}
u K_0^j+\pi K_0^n$. The remainder's total mass is the stationary probability of no successful coin in its first $n$ opportunities, which tends to zero by step 2.1 and monotone convergence. Therefore the potential measure $\eta=\sum_{j\ge0}
u K_0^j$ equals $\pi/p$. It counts every core state before its fresh coin is sampled, including the state of the terminal successful coin. In particular $\mathbb E\ell=\eta(S)=1/p$ and $\mathbb EL=m/p$.

